    {
      "id": "claim_1f931ed340c24e66ac3b3f8333417062",
      "statement": "A hand-authored annotation schema is an array of AnnotationDef nodes under config.schema; resolveSchema(defs) validates and resolves them into ResolvedDef[] with defaults applied (min/max to 1/1-or-null, required forced false on booleans, visibleIf dropped unless it names a real answerable sibling or a straight ancestor), an id assigned from the slash-joined name path, and children recursively resolved.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/model/schema.ts#L400-L483",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:48c593347082e1537d17a0ce171e433f75ea824c69f77eb02a3cd6802f2d9132:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d046d9299e8d46dcb780e184aa901410",
      "statement": "resolveSchema enforces structural rules at every level: sibling names must be unique (they key the saved data), siblings differing only by surrounding whitespace are rejected because the canonical path cannot tell them apart, and a field named __proto__ is refused because Object.prototype's setter would silently drop its answers on save.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/model/schema.ts#L411-L447",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6d706b1d61a433a83554aa73fc21a09950eac05630840ba01c2097ced7f0ca0a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_653f710acea9469e952ab87f85fd22d1",
      "statement": "resolveSchema refuses a schema whose empty tree would materialize more than 100000 instances before any input, because min is a lower bound and initTree/normalizeTree materialize max(min,1) instances per node recursively at load; nested groups multiply, so a per-node min cap cannot stop the nested case and the product down each branch is bounded directly.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/model/schema.ts#L485-L520",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0be264bb5a74d3b487475f1a1b364d27ac5c437c7f103e05f0d3903773bca9b0:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_6a23ddfda1cd4087918c4f0b279b330c",
      "statement": "FieldType is 'string' | 'number' | 'boolean' | 'year'; 'year' rides the same on-disk shape as 'number' (a JSON number) but is range-validated against the static YEAR_MIN..YEAR_MAX (1000-2100), and validating type against a fixed enum means a 'year' field fails to load in an older SaiLoR that predates the type.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/model/schema.ts#L11-L17",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e44e38ce2fb00fe2cde14b7a03631f6fd9d5ef789f2193d9c2773937947393ae:"
